    "code_current_through_note": "Adopted November 17, 2025, effective November 22, 2025 (title page). No amendments listed on the Township site (Land Use and News pages read 2026-11-13).",
    "code_caution": "In the C-MDR district (906.B.2 and B.3) the side and rear yard figures repeat the lot width figures (for example 150 ft side and rear yards for a single-family house without both public utilities). This looks like a drafting error, but it is the law as printed. With 80 ft side yards a typical 80 ft wide C-MDR lot has no buildable width, so an addition or a detached unit cannot meet them. Only a unit inside the existing house works without relief. Ask the Township before relying on C-MDR yards. Board of Supervisors minutes since adoption were not checked for amendments.",
    "checks": [
      "An ADU here is only for close relatives who need care: at most two persons, relatives of the permanent residents of the house, at least one needing the unit because of illness, old age or disability (Art. 2 'Accessory Dwelling Unit', 1502.H.1.a)",
      "A permitted accessory use in AP, LC, RR, SFR, C-MDR, V and I (sections 505, 605, 705, 805, 905, 1005, 1105) and in the IO overlay where the underlying district allows it (1205). Zoning permit from the Zoning Officer",
      "The unit must be designed to be easily turned back into part of the house, removed, or turned into a lawful accessory use when the relative leaves. A legally binding document acceptable to the Township, binding on future owners, bars its use as a separate dwelling (1502.H.1.b, c)",
      "The unit is attached to the house, with an interior door between the two, unless the Township specifically approves a detached unit. A detached unit must meet the principal building setbacks and be removed within 90 days after the relative leaves. A lawful detached garage may be converted and later turned back (1502.H.1.b, d)",
      "It may not change the single-family look of the house from the property lines (1502.H.1.d)",
      "An on-lot septic system must be re-certified if sewage flow will increase (1502.H.1.e)",
      "Parking: one space for the ADU, plus two for the house (1602.H.1, 1602.B.9)",
      "No size cap for the unit",
      "A new detached unit needs the Township's specific approval (1502.H.1.d). The code names no body and no procedure. The tool shows it as a conditional use, the nearest path, but no hearing is named. Ask the Township",
      "A converted lawful detached garage may later be turned back into a garage or home occupation area. The 90-day removal and the principal-setback rule are written for a detached dwelling placed on the lot (1502.H.1.b, d). Ask whether the specific approval also applies to a garage conversion",
      "Detached unit height: 15 ft at the 5 ft accessory setback, plus 1 ft for every 2 ft of extra setback, up to 25 ft. A detached unit sits at the principal setbacks, so at the side yard it gets about 17.5 ft in SFR, 20 ft in AP and RR (and in V without both public utilities), 25 ft in LC and C-MDR, and 15 ft in V with both utilities (1402.F.4, 1402.D.2.b(1), 1502.H.1.d)",
      "No accessory structure in a required front yard (1402.D.2.a)",
      "IO is an overlay that keeps the underlying district's residential uses (1201.B, 1202.B.1, 1205.A). Use the underlying district's rules",
      "In AP the number of dwellings and lots is fixed by the size of the deeded area (506.A). Ask whether a detached unit counts against it",
      "A lot in a residential district may hold only one principal use (1402.A.2)",
      "Duplex dwellings are a use by right only in C-MDR. Conversion apartments (three or more units) are special exceptions in AP, LC, RR, C-MDR and V. Barn conversion apartments are special exceptions in AP, LC, RR and SFR (902, 503, 603, 703, 803, 903, 1003)",
      "Uses not expressly permitted elsewhere may be a conditional use (1502.I). A second unrestricted dwelling is a duplex, which is permitted in C-MDR, so that path does not reach it",
      "Vacation rentals are a special exception use with their own standards (1502.C.19). The relative rule leaves no room for renting the ADU"
    ],
    "notes": "Zoning office: Highland Township, Adams County (GEOID 4200134424). Read the adopted PDF in full text. Searched for accessory dwelling, accessory apartment, relative, duplex, conversion, similar, not expressly, short-term, vacation rental, nonconforming. 'Accessory Apartment' is defined in Article 2 but used nowhere in the districts. District codes: AP, LC, RR, SFR, C-MDR, V, I, IO overlay, FO floodplain overlay."
